- [builder:claude-b] Goal seek and What matters most (was Sensitivity) stop treating a higher return as a fix, and start simple: the return the plan would need is one short grey line set against forecasts for the plan's own mix, with no button, its detail one tap away, and no figure when growth does not matter; Goal seek shows three change cards first (what is worth money first), the rest, room for bad luck, an amount of your own and Social Security's ages one quiet tap away, and its card titles fit at 320 px; the saving card names a 401(k) with nothing going in and gives the amount that works typed there (up to the yearly limit, the rest into other savings); the Social Security card on a short plan says whether that age alone gets there or when the money would then run out; the retirement card is never "room to spare" while the money runs short; What matters most says "We don't know yet" with no savings on file, shows the three numbers that move the plan most and never lists one that moves nothing among them (it says "no change here" in the fold, and measures how long the money lasts when the plan can pay for no steady spending), keeps its other measures and each row's detail one tap away, shows how much you save in dollars when nothing goes in, and its headline says what to do; Legacy goals no longer lists the return, shows three changes first and folds the optional note.
